BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Nerd Nite Bloomington
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260925T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260925T213000
UID:2cf7d1e417b7a10a5d97f790c6bdc3c6@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for our sixth Nerd Nite Bloomington!\nDoors at 7:00pm 
 | Presentations at 7:30\nWe all know that learning is more fun when you’
 re drinking with friends and colleagues. Nerd Nite is an event held in mor
 e than 120 cities across the globe during which several folks give 15 minu
 te fun-yet-informative presentations across all disciplines – while the 
 audience drinks along. It’s like the Discovery Channel… with beer! Ima
 gine learning about everything from math feuds or the science of the Simps
 ons\, to the genealogy of Godzilla or debunking beer myths\, while having 
 a few or a few too many.\nCome join us for a drink\, learn something new\,
  and meet fellow nerds. Be there AND be square!\nThis month's speakers and
  presentation topics:\n1) Sex on Six Legs: The Secret Lives of Wasps and F
 lies\nby Kylie Dannatt\nInsects are the most diverse group of animals on t
 he planet accounting for more than half of all known living species on Ear
 th. Bug sex\, like bugs themselves\, is quite diverse. From detachable pen
 ises\, loud sex that becomes fatal\, and sexual cannibalism\, sex on six l
 egs is never boring by human standards. What do thistle tortoise beetles a
 nd the tuberous bush cricket have in common? Grab a drink and find out!\n2
 ) In Pursuit of the Perfect Map\nby Andy Petersen\nWhether for exploring t
 he world\, claiming territory\, or the much-beloved practice of collecting
  taxes\, maps have been shaping and reshaping our societies for thousands 
 of years. However much we try though\, our maps always have inaccuracies
 —whether intentional or not. Together we'll (very) briefly examine the h
 istory of maps\, consider the approaches to address these inaccuracies\, a
 nd try to determine what is the perfect map.\n3) Malicious Molasses: The S
 tickiest Situation in American History?\nby Molly Beausir\nBoston has been
  host to some of the most major moments in American History. But you might
  not think to visit the site of a disaster of sticky proportions right off
  the Freedom Trail that resulted in the deaths of 21 people and a lawsuit 
 that forever changed the landscape of corporations' accountability to the 
 public in the United States. Fair warning: You'll never be able to look at
  a jar of molasses the same again.
GEO:39.1657566;-86.53334079999999
LOCATION:The Bishop\, 123 S. Walnut Street\, Bloomington\, IN 47404
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/nerd-nite-bloomington/59594/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
