DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260930T230000
UID:55ddf520d1ff445f908be0f180d238eb@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:The essential goal of Conversations in Bloom: A Symposium on A
 rt\, Community\, and Memory is to create a community forum for talking ab
 out community-making through the arts in Bloomington. The conceptual ancho
 rs of the program are arts\, community\, and memory\, which serve as throu
 gh-lines for thinking about the interplay between shared and individual ex
 periences\, work\, and histories. Conversation and collaboration are the b
 eating hearts of this program. All of the sessions and events were designe
 d in collaboration with participating community partners over many months 
 of intentional conversation and dialogue. Throughout the planning we pushe
 d ourselves and our community partners to critically examine how our engag
 ement with the arts helps us process the world around us and collectively 
 produce a sense of community and animates memory in ways that help build t
 owards shared futures. We look forward to continuing the conversation with
  you all.
GEO:39.1662103;-86.53849430000001
LOCATION:I Fell Gallery and Studios\; FAR Center for Contemporary Arts\; L
 otus Education and Arts Foundation\, 105 S Rogers St\, Bloomington\, IN 47
 404
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/conversations-in-bloom-a-sympos
 ium-on-art-community-and-memory/59891/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
