BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Best Little Whorehouse in Texas | Additional Films and Guests
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260930T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260930T210000
UID:9caaa3ad61eca23af2745152f599f7fa@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:When a pious television "reporter" Melvin P. Thorpe (Dom DeLui
 se) threatens to expose Miss Mona's (Dolly Parton) Texas brothel—the Chi
 cken Ranch—to public scandal and close it down for good\, she vows not t
 o go down without a fight! With the help of her long-time secret sweetie S
 heriff Ed Earl Dodd (Burt Reynolds)\, the two join together to keep the ra
 nch open and\, naturally\, deepen their own romance along the way. Sing al
 ong through this extraordinary story about passion\, scandal\, community\,
  and resistance! First premiering as a Broadway musical in 1978\, The Best
  Little Whorehouse in Texas film adaptation was a critical mixed bag upon 
 its release\, but the people loved it! The film brought in the biggest wee
 kend box-office opening for a musical up to that point in time and was nom
 inated for two Golden Globes: Best Motion Picture - Musical or Comedy and 
 Best Actress in a Motion Picture or Comedy for Parton. Musical numbers inc
 lude two of Parton's biggest hits: "Hard Candy Christmas" and "I Will Alwa
 ys Love You." [114 min\; comedy\, musical\, romance\; English]
GEO:39.168585;-86.517361
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 E. 7th Street\, Bloomington\, IN 47405
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/the-best-little-whorehouse-in-t
 exas-additional-films-and-guests/59733/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Treasures of the Silk Road
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260930T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260930T180000
UID:c87a42be599988353116cb3610c42d05@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:The McCalla Center\, in collaboration with musician and schola
 r Shahyar Daneshgar\, celebrates the opening of its new exhibition Treasur
 es of the Silk Road on Friday\, September 25th\, 4:00 pm-6:00 pm EDT.\nThe
  exhibit features over 70 musical instruments from the Pastel-Daneshgar mu
 sical instrument collection\, with a focus on strings\, flutes\, and percu
 ssion from across Asia\, the Middle East\, and North Africa. Crafted from 
 wood\, snakeskin\, horsehair\, lambskin\, camel bone\, and other unique ma
 terials\, these instruments provide a compelling history of cultural and a
 rtistic exchanges that have led to the myriad musical sounds and styles th
 at permeate the world today. The opening event will feature remarks from t
 he collection owner\, Shahyar Daneshgar\, and will feature musical clips p
 rovided by the Lotus World Music & Arts Festival.\nShahyar Daneshgar is a 
 lifelong musician\, scholar\, and cultural ambassador whose passion for tr
 aditional music has shaped more than three decades of collecting\, teachin
 g\, and performing. Born into a large musical family\, he studied at the T
 ehran Conservatory of Music before pursuing academic work in Germany and l
 ater at Indiana University\, where he earned his Ph.D. in Central Eurasian
  Studies in 1995. He taught at Indiana University until his retirement in 
 2024. He is founder and director of the Bloomington Silk Road Ensemble.\nT
 he exhibition is free and runs from September 25\, 2026\, to September 202
 7.\nThe mission of the McCalla Center is to provide accessible exhibition 
 and educational experiences\, creating opportunities for students\, facult
 y\, and the community to engage with collections\, IU-generated creative a
 ctivity\, and community projects in meaningful and innovative ways.
GEO:39.1709246;-86.527549
LOCATION:McCalla Center\, McCalla Center\, 525 E. 9th Street\, Bloomington
 \, IN 47408
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/treasures-of-the-silk-road/5960
 4/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Waitress
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260930T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260930T213000
UID:2a2fa07eecb75b5726b985fa1865623a@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:Meet Jenna\, a waitress and expert pie maker who dreams of a w
 ay out of her small town and rocky marriage. Pouring her heart into her pi
 es\, she crafts desserts that mirror her topsy-turvy life such as “The K
 ey (Lime) to Happiness Pie” and “Betrayed by My Eggs Pie.” When a ba
 king contest in a nearby county (and a satisfying encounter with someone n
 ew) show Jenna a chance at a fresh start\, she must find the courage to se
 ize it. Change is on the menu\, as long as Jenna can write her own perfect
 ly personal recipe for happiness.\n Brought to life by a groundbreaking cr
 eative team\, this hilarious hit Broadway musical features original music 
 and lyrics by Grammy Award winner Sara Bareilles (“Brave\,” “Love So
 ng”)\, a book by acclaimed screenwriter Jessie Nelson (I Am Sam)\, origi
 nal choreography by Lorin Latarro (Mrs. Doubtfire\, Chess) and original di
 rection by Tony Award winner Diane Paulus (1776\, Jagged Little Pill\, Pip
 pin).\n “Waitress is a little slice of heaven!” says Entertainment Wee
 kly\, and is “sweet\, sassy and passionate\,” according to New York Ma
 gazine.\n “It’s an empowering musical of the highest order!” raves t
 he Chicago Tribune. Don’t miss this uplifting and hilarious musical cele
 brating friendship\, motherhood\, and the magic of a well-made pie.
GEO:39.1684021;-86.5178918
LOCATION:Indiana University Auditorium\, 1211 E 7th St\, Bloomington\, IN 
 47405
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/waitress/58925/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
