DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261001T200000
UID:16bc652e2ad1fea3e7a831810f44f19e@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:Do you remember a time when coffee shops would stay open late 
 and you'd get to listen to spoken word or a musician strumming a guitar an
 d singing harmonies from a chair across the room\, while sipping on someth
 ing sweet and being across from folks you either just met or have known fo
 r a lifetime? \nIs that just me? \nEither way\, let's do that again? \nOn 
 third Wednesdays we stay open late for Downtown Shop - an event that local
  retailers have been hosting where folks can come downtown and experience 
 a later shopping hour complete with specials\, pop-ups\, cocktails and mor
 e. For us -- we're hosting musicians\, spoken word\, and more. Come in\, r
 elax\, take a break in the middle of the week like you deserve. Grab a cof
 fee\, a matcha\, or CBD beverage and just vibe with the soulful sounds of 
 music playing through the plants. \nWe welcome you. Every third Wednesday 
 here at oak. \nIn September we welcome Truth and Consequences - a beautifu
 l local duo with an angelic voice and beautiful harmonies.
GEO:39.167879;-86.53442559999999
LOCATION:oak.\, 116 W 6th Street\, Suite 101\, Bloomington\, IN 47401
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/late-nights-at-the-coffeeshop-l
 ive-musicdowntown-shop/59622/
