UID:ab7a115cfbf93ad70e4fd764df2f49b3@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:First Thursdays showcase the diversity of arts and humanities 
 at IU Bloomington and offer a welcoming environment for students\, faculty
 \, staff\, and community members to explore new creative outlets. Each eve
 nt is a unique opportunity to experience the wonderful work of artists\, p
 erformers\, and scholars from across campus and around town. \nThe October
  First Thursdays will be a festival highlighting the work of arts & humani
 ties groups on campus and in the community. The event is free and open to 
 the public and will feature 90+ a&h-focused activity booths\, 35+ arts & c
 rafts vendors\, performances\, extended gallery hours\, food trucks\, give
 aways\, and more. Around the IU Fine Arts Plaza\, there will be activities
  and performances paying tribute to the late Dolly Parton\, a “make your
  own monster” craft station\, a mobile blood drive\, and animal ambassad
 ors\, among many other activities. On the main stage\, we’ll have perfor
 mances by Tipa Tipo\, Bloomington Delta Music Club\, IU Musical Theatre\, 
 and an interactive Bad Bunny Pilates demonstration! \nFirst Thursdays are 
 hosted by the IU Arts & Humanities Council. For more information and volun
 teer opportunities\, please visit go.iu.edu/first-thursdays.
GEO:39.1690552;-86.5189588
