BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fall Ballet
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261002
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261003
UID:d316780f9dcd56ed67e791da5e3667a2@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:White Shadows\nChristian Claessens\nLongtime Jacobs faculty me
 mber Christian Claessens teams up with the Jacobs Percussion Department to
  create this world premiere based on the last three movements of Steve Rei
 ch’s Sextet\, employing marimbas\, vibraphones\, bass drums\, and more. 
 The eight dancers embody movement from pulsations to melodic patterns to r
 hythmic ambiguity.\nChristian Claessens\, Choreographer\nJoseph Gramley\, 
 Conductor and Chamber Music Coach\nBlake Kile\, Lighting Designer\nValse-F
 antaisie\nGeorge Balanchine\nAttended by their single partner\, five balle
 rinas move in a whirl of perpetual motion to Mikhail Glinka’s waltzing r
 hythms. Although it was popularly called “the Melancholy Waltz\,” this
  1967 rendering is fast and light and was originally presented as the seco
 nd section of Glinkiana\, which featured former IU Distinguished Professor
  Violette Verdy in its New York City Ballet premiere.\nGeorge Balanchine\,
  Choreographer\nKyra Nichols\, Stager\nBlake Kile\, Lighting Designer\nDig
 nity in Restraint\nCaili Quan\nBorn to a Chamorro Filipino family in Guam\
 , Caili Quan created this punchy work on New York City Ballet dancers to B
 eethoven’s String Quartet No. 12. Her love for “showing people the mus
 ic” is on full display as she corresponds five major chords to the five 
 core emotions of anger\, fear\, disgust\, joy\, and sadness.\nCaili Quan\,
  Choreographer\nAndrea Yorita\, Stager\nBlake Kile\, Lighting Designer\nWo
 rld Premiere\nJames Whiteside\nA principal dancer and choreographer with A
 merican Ballet Theatre\, James Whiteside is also a pop music performer\, m
 odel\, drag queen\, podcast host\, and author. He brings his wildly eclect
 ic style to Jacobs for several weeks as he creates his latest work\, with 
 the students of the Ballet Department.\nJames Whiteside\, Choreographer\nM
 ichael Breeden\, Stager\nBlake Kile\, Lighting Designer
GEO:39.1665575;-86.51751229999999
LOCATION:Musical Arts Center\, 101 N Eagleson Ave\, Bloomington\, IN 47406
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/fall-ballet/59542/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
