BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Such Now the Necessity: The Declaration and Secession
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261002T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261002T150000
UID:48e4ec76563444076ef508ba331bfa04@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:The symposium “Such Now the Necessity: The Declaration and S
 ecession” is scheduled for 2 October\, from 10:00am to 3:00pm\, in the I
 MU Federal Room. The symposium considers the Declaration specifically as a
  secessionist document: how it functioned in the early United States\, how
  it relates to broader theories of secession\, and how it has been or migh
 t be used in other political contexts.\nThe Declaration of Independence is
  revered as the formative expression of American values. However\, it was 
 designed primarily as a legal and rhetorical address to the world—"to th
 e opinions of mankind"—justifying a radical project: secession. The Decl
 aration advances the two principal arguments that are familiar justificati
 ons used by secession movements today: an inherent right to self-governmen
 t based on "consent of the governed\," and "remedial secession" in respons
 e to "a long train of abuses." Given this founding DNA\, why is the United
  States no longer a pro-secession advocate? What would it mean to take the
  Declaration’s arguments seriously today—both in America’s foreign r
 elations and for America’s own territories (such as Puerto Rico) and the
  50 states?
GEO:39.1677781;-86.52366049999999
LOCATION:IMU Federal Room\, 900 E. 7th Street\, Bloomington\, IN 47405
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/such-now-the-necessity-the-decl
 aration-and-secession/59940/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
