 today. Filled with celebrations\, overdue realizations\, and lessons for f
 uture generations\, Tomorrow’s Sentry reminds us that today’s youth wi
 ll become tomorrow’s guardians of history.
GEO:39.1657967;-86.5339376
LOCATION:Waldron Arts Center\, 122 S. Walnut St.\, Bloomington\, IN 47404
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/tomorrows-sentry/59374/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:War Paint: Women at War | Art and a Movie
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261004T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261004T143000
UID:7403be54b70b95c67f15b73af55dcc9e@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:Margy Kinmonth’s feature documentary shines a light on the t
 railblazing role of women war artists\, on the frontlines round the world\
 , championing the female perspective on conflict through art. Culture brea
 ks the taboo\, crosses borders—tells the truth to power. Artists discuss
 ed include: Zhanna Kadyrova\, Linda Kitson\, Shirin Neshat\, Rachel Reckit
 t\, Dame Laura Knight\, Lee Miller\, Nina Berman\, Marcelle Hanselaar\, Ja
 nanne Al-Ani\, Assil Diab\, Doris Zinkeisen\, Fiona Banner aka The Vanity 
 Press\, Maggi Hambling\, Cornelia Parker\, Dame Rachel Whiteread\, Maya Li
 n\, and including the work of Anne Desmet R.A.\, Samar Hussaini\, and feat
 uring Dame Penelope Lively\, Charlotte Johnstone\, and Ami Bouhassane. A c
 ast of women contributors and crew makes this film a unique undertaking\, 
 telling vital truths in turbulent times. War Paint: Women at War is the th
 ird installment in Kinmonth’s trilogy of films about how artists depict 
 war\, following the acclaimed Eric Ravilious: Drawn to War and War Art wit
 h Eddie Redmayne. [89 min\; documentary\, war\; English]\nThis program is 
 presented in partnership with the Eskenazi Museum of Art. After the screen
 ing\, continue the conversation at the Eskenazi Museum of Art with a speci
 al program led by museum photographer Shanti Knight.
GEO:39.168585;-86.517361
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 E. 7th Street\, Bloomington\, IN 47405
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/war-paint-women-at-war-art-and-
 a-movie/59839/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
