BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:An Evening with Sutton Foster
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261006T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261006T213000
UID:5641c640f3d69dcf2518495a9e9f6bf5@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:Sutton Foster is a two-time Tony Award-winning actress\, singe
 r\, and dancer widely recognized as one of Broadway’s leading performers
 . For her Bloomington performance\, she will be joined onstage by IU dance
  and choral students along with local K-12 performers for what promises to
  be a special evening.\n Foster most recently starred as Princess Winnifre
 d in Once Upon a Mattress  during its acclaimed Broadway revival. Prior\,
  she starred as Mrs. Lovett in the Tony Award-winning Broadway revival of
   Sweeney Todd: The Demon Barber of Fleet Street \, as well as Marian Par
 oo in the 2022 Broadway revival of  The Music Man \, earning her seventh 
 Tony Award nomination.\n She first rose to prominence originating the titl
 e role in Broadway’s Thoroughly Modern Millie \, earning her first Tony 
 Award\, and later won her second for  Anything Goes . Her extensive stage
  credits include  The Drowsy Chaperone \,  Shrek the Musical \,  Young 
 Frankenstein \,  Violet \, and  Sweet Charity. \n On screen\, Foster sta
 rred in TV Land’s Younger  and appeared in  Bunheads\, Gilmore Girls: 
 A Year in the Life \, and the final season of  The Marvelous Mrs. Maisel 
 . As a solo artist\, she has toured the country with stops at Carnegie Hal
 l\, Feinstein’s\, Lincoln Center’s American Songbook series\, and many
  others. Foster holds an honorary doctorate from Ball State University\, w
 here she also teaches.
GEO:39.1684021;-86.5178918
LOCATION:Indiana University Auditorium\, 1211 E 7th St\, Bloomington\, IN 
 47405
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/an-evening-with-sutton-foster/5
 8916/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
