BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mangrove School + Makongo/Caterpillars w/ Q&A | For All the Childr
 en
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261006T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261006T211500
UID:ca00c72992c87c7ea37d76eecae4e37b@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:Mangrove School (Filipa César and Sónia Vaz Borges\, Guinea 
 Bissau\, 2022): During the anticolonial struggle against Portuguese occupa
 tion\, the free schools in Guinea Bissau moved deep into the jungle and fo
 und the mangroves. The schools were fashioned on the interwoven branches a
 nd roots. The directors film the mangroves as an infrastructure with a net
 worked architecture\, as the locus of transmission\, of radical education\
 , attentive to the memory of the struggles. The mangrove's branches are po
 werful and encourage networks\, collectives\, and horizontality. [35 min\;
  documentary\; Portuguese with English subtitles]\nMakongo/Caterpillars (E
 lvis Sabin Ngaïbino\, Central African Republic\, 2020): Albert and André
  strive to create a school in their forest community in equatorial Central
  African Republic. As the only secondary school graduates in their village
 \, they teach local children while relying on the annual makongo (caterpil
 lar) harvest to fund their project. This vivid ethnographic portrait offer
 s no embellishment\, no narration\, and no added music. The direct cinema 
 approach is remarkably sensitive\, attuned to the sounds of animals\, the 
 rain forest\, and the daily life of the men and their families. [73 min\; 
 documentary\; Sango and French with English subtitles]\nA Q&A will follow 
 the screening.
GEO:39.168585;-86.517361
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 E. 7th Street\, Bloomington\, IN 47405
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/mangrove-school-makongocaterpil
 lars-w-qa-for-all-the-children/59841/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
