BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Talking Conservation: Indiana’s Lake Michigan Shoreline and the 
 Public Trust Doctrine in Action
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261007T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261007T191500
UID:1b0089df38f42452641ed4885626c1c9@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:Talking Conservation is a public lecture series hosted by Cons
 ervation Law Center in Bloomington\, Indiana\, exploring the ideas\, peopl
 e\, and legal frameworks shaping the future of land\, water\, wildlife\, a
 nd healthy communities. This series is designed to be welcoming\, practica
 l\, and rooted in real-world challenges and solutions—grounded in Indian
 a\, while connected to broader regional and national conversations. \nIn t
 his lecture\, Paul Labovitz will introduce the Indiana Dunes National Park
 \, Indiana’s most visited tourist attraction and talk about the importan
 ce of providing public access to this globally significant place. He will 
 connect the tradition of how the National Park Service preserves and prote
 cts “in perpetuity” America’s most important natural and cultural tr
 easures for “the enjoyment\, education and inspiration of this and futur
 e generations” with Gunderson v State\, the 2018 Indiana Supreme Court u
 nanimous decision that the State owns the bed and shoreline of Lake Michig
 an up to the Ordinary High-Water Mark in public trust. Paul will talk abou
 t why public access Is not only sound ecological practice but also a signi
 ficant economic factor in the region and state economy. There will be a fe
 w stories from Paul’s tenure as the National Park Superintendent and ple
 nty of time for questions and discussion. \nThis event is free and open to
  the public\, but registration is required. A reception with snacks and be
 verages will follow the lecture. Learn more and register online at https:/
 /conservationlawcenter.org/talkingconservation/
GEO:39.1663072;-86.53169650000001
LOCATION:Graduate by Hilton Bloomington\, 210 E Kirkwood Ave\, Bloomington
 \, IN 47408
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/talking-conservation-indianas-l
 ake-michigan-shoreline-and-the-public-trust-doctrine-in-action/59609/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Flying Ace w/ Q&A | Additional Films and Guests
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261007T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261007T203000
UID:6836f22710b1726a8a461dec3a9fe6f6@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:The Flying Ace is an aspirational "race film\," chronicling a 
 Black WWI fighter pilot who\, after honorably serving\, returns to his civ
 ilian job as a railroad detective. He uses his military training and detec
 tive skills to find and capture a gang of railroad thieves who stole $25\,
 000 from his company. Shot at a time when racism and segregation prevented
  Black people from becoming pilots in the armed forces and when Hollywood 
 continually portrayed Black people as one-dimensional caricatures\, The Fl
 ying Ace empowers Black people and features multi-dimensional representati
 ons of Black life\, culture\, and identities. The film was directed by Ric
 hard E. Norman and stars Laurence Criner\, Katherine Boyd\, and Steve "Peg
 " Reynolds. The Flying Ace is the lone surviving film made at Richard E. N
 orman's Jacksonville\, FL-based Norman Studios\, and this year marks the c
 entennial of its release. Fully restored by the Library of Congress\, the 
 film was selected for the National Film Registry in 2021. [65 min\; myster
 y\, adventure\; silent with English title cards]\nA Q&A with Black Film Ce
 nter & Archive Director Novotny Lawrence and ReelAbilities Director of Eng
 agement Lawrence Carter-Long will follow the screening.
GEO:39.168585;-86.517361
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 E. 7th Street\, Bloomington\, IN 47405
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/the-flying-ace-w-qa-additional-
 films-and-guests/59842/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
