BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Two Prosecuters | Arthouse Now
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261008T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261008T210000
UID:4f1a8ba74dfea5d2e4ff94201f42f62a@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:Adapted from a novel by Soviet writer/political prisoner Georg
 y Demidov and set in the Soviet Union in 1937\, Two Prosecutors follows th
 e attempts of an idealistic government-appointed prosecutor to expose the 
 mistreatment of a dissident Bolshevik writer who has been jailed and tortu
 red without evidence of wrongdoing. He soon realizes the lack of cause for
  the man's imprisonment isn’t unique under Stalin\, and the young lawyer
 ’s moral righteousness may be putting himself in danger. Constructed wit
 h a patient yet unmistakable sense of mounting dread\, the film exposes ho
 w the minutiae of everyday enables fascism’s function. [118 min\; drama\
 ; Russian and Ukrainian with English subtitles]
GEO:39.168585;-86.517361
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 E. 7th Street\, Bloomington\, IN 47405
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/two-prosecuters-arthouse-now/59
 843/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
