BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:David Kaser Endowed Lecture Series Presents: Dr. Safiya Noble "AI 
 and Our Future: How Artificial Intelligence and Search Engine Algorithms R
 einforce Oppression"
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261023T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261023T130000
UID:17364b61856ac3e56ee6e6b20d7588d2@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:The landscape of information is rapidly shifting as new impera
 tives and demands push to the fore increasing investment in digital techno
 logies. Yet\, critical information scholars continue to demonstrate how di
 gital technology and its narratives are shaped by and infused with values 
 that are not impartial. Technologies consist of a set of social practices\
 , situated within the dynamics of race\, gender\, class\, and politics\, a
 nd in the service of something -- a position\, a profit motive\, a means t
 o an end. In this talk\, Dr. Safiya Umoja Noble will discuss her book\, Al
 gorithms of Oppression\, and delve into issues ranging from marginalizatio
 n and misrepresentation in commercial information platforms like Google se
 arch\, to the profound power struggles that violate civil\, human\, and co
 llective rights through AI and machine learning projects.
GEO:39.1727224;-86.5232788
LOCATION:Indiana Memorial Union Whittenberger Auditorium\, 700 N Woodlawn 
 Ave\, Bloomington\, IN 47408
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/david-kaser-endowed-lecture-ser
 ies-presents-dr-safiya-noble-ai-and-our-future-how-artificial-intelligence
 -and-search-engine-algorithms-reinforce-oppression/59820/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Don't Look Now | Friday Night Frights
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261023T220000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261024T000000
UID:7b89190373d1ec3db98b414143df201b@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:Adapted from a Daphne du Maurier short story\, Don't Look Now 
 follows John (Donald Sutherland) and Christine (Julie Christie)\, still gr
 ieving over the accidental death of their daughter\, as they head to Venic
 e for John's work restoring a church. Soon\, Laura meets two sisters who c
 laim to be in touch with the spirit of their dead daughter and the couple 
 must decide what is real\, what is supernatural\, and what is somewhere in
 -between. Renowned for innovative editing style\, memorable recurring aest
 hetic motifs\, an impressionistic formal style\, and nonlinear storytellin
 g that destabilizes the viewer\, the film was controversial on its release
  but is now considered a classic\, landing multiples times on Sight and So
 und’s list of the best films of all time\, the BFI list of greatest Brit
 ish films\, and was reevaluated by Roget Ebert as an occult-horror classic
 . Don’t Look Now has also inspired filmmakers like Danny Boyle\, Lynne R
 amsey\, Ari Aster\, Steven Soderbergh\, and many more. [110 min\; horror\;
  English and Italian]
GEO:39.168585;-86.517361
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 E. 7th Street\, Bloomington\, IN 47405
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/dont-look-now-friday-night-frig
 hts/59861/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
