BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:And So I Stayed w/ filmmaker | Additional Films and Guests
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261024T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261024T210000
UID:2eae34bcd4cf187b3b414b477ac1d87d@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:And So I Stayed is an award-winning documentary by Natalie Pat
 tillo and Daniel A. Nelson about survivors of abuse fighting for their liv
 es and spending years behind bars. It is a moving portrait of Kim\, Tanish
 a\, and Nikki\, three survivors whose strikingly similar stories are separ
 ated by over 30 years. None of them were believed\, and each of them was c
 riminalized for fighting back. This film is made for and by survivors. For
  them and us to feel heard\, seen\, and believed. [91 min\; documentary\; 
 English]\nA panel discussion and Q&A will follow the screening with co-dir
 ector Natalie Pattillo\, Kerry Hyatt Bennett (Chief Legal Counsel\, IN Coa
 lition Against Domestic Violence)\, and Carrie Stillions (Executive Direct
 or\, Middle Way House)\, moderated by Zoe Peterson (Senior Scientist\, Kin
 sey Institute\; Professor of Applied Psychology\, Education and Research M
 ethodology).
GEO:39.168585;-86.517361
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 E. 7th Street\, Bloomington\, IN 47405
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/and-so-i-stayed-w-filmmaker-add
 itional-films-and-guests/59863/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bloomington Pumpkin Launch
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261024T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261024T140000
UID:d77017537a785795c2e73deb22ea395c@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:Watch pumpkins soar through the sky\, or build your own launch
 er to join the fun! The Bloomington Pumpkin Launch is a one-of-a-kind fall
  tradition where creativity\, engineering\, and pumpkins collide. \n Gath
 er friends\, fellow club members\, or colleagues and design your own pumpk
 in-flinging machine. Whether it is powered by physics\, tension\, or pure 
 imagination\, we would love to see it on the launch line. \n No launch de
 vice? No problem! There is still plenty to enjoy. Spectators cheer on thei
 r favorite teams\, marvel at pumpkin drops from a bucket truck\, and soak 
 up the festive fall vibes that include live music\, autumn-themed activiti
 es for kids\, food vendors\, and more. Bring a lawn chair and spend the da
 y watching pumpkins fly!\n Launcher Divisions\nYouth Human Powered (elemen
 tary or middle school)\nStudent Human Powered (high school or college)\nAd
 ult Human Powered\nLauncher Size Classes\nLarge - (pumpkins must be 5 lbs 
 or more)\nSmall - (pumpkins should be 2-4 lbs)\nMini - (pumpkins should be
  less than 2 lbs and all launcher components must fit entirely in a single
  vehicle such as a pickup truck\, small van\, or SUV)\nLaunching Device Re
 quirements\nCannons and chemically powered launchers are NOT permitted. De
 vice must be mechanical only. No fuel\, compressed air\, electricity\, exp
 losives\, and/or other chemical components or any other fluids including b
 ut not limited to oil\, water\, and hydraulic fluid allowed. The only exce
 ption is for a small powered winch on the machine to help cock the throwin
 g arm.\nA safety strap or other mechanism is required to remain in place a
 t all times on the throwing arm after the machine is cocked until released
  for firing. This is to ensure that no premature launches occur.\nAny devi
 ce constructed similar to a catapult must launch overhand\, and not sidear
 m.\nCompetitions\nTeams compete in both accuracy and distance contests. Ea
 ch contest consists of four rounds of launching.\nTeams must bring a minim
 um of eight pumpkins weighing between 5 and 8 pounds to the competition.\n
 Launcher team registration deadline is Wednesday\, Oct. 16. There is no fe
 e to register a launcher.\n For more information about the Pumpkin Launch\
 , email Bill Ream or call 812-349-3748.
GEO:39.137016;-86.6064789
LOCATION:Monroe County Fairgrounds\, 5700 W. Airport Road\, Bloomington\, 
 IN 47403
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/bloomington-pumpkin-launch/5958
 2/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
