BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Everybody to Kenmure Street | Arthouse Now
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261027T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261027T204500
UID:78a2441cf389c42240c445d1937bd3a4@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:The first day of Eid in Glasgow started as any other. But soon
 \, neighbors heard through community message networks that two local men w
 ere snatched up for deportation\, and suddenly hundreds of people left the
 ir breakfast tables\, work Zoom calls\, and daily lives to rush down to Ke
 nmure Street to save them by putting their bodies on the line. Though most
 ly strangers\, and with almost no planning\, this extremely diverse group 
 organized themselves\, taking on essential roles to allow the collective t
 o protect their own from government forces targeting their least protected
  neighbors. An inspiring and profoundly moving portrait of what we all are
  capable of in the face of injustice\, Everybody to Kenmure Street reminds
  us of the power that is always inherent in the people. Winner\, World Cin
 ema Documentary Special Jury Award for Civil Resistance\, Sundance Film Fe
 stival 2026. [95 min\; documentary\; English]
GEO:39.168585;-86.517361
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 E. 7th Street\, Bloomington\, IN 47405
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/everybody-to-kenmure-street-art
 house-now/59866/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
