 nd be a part of making film for all possible!\nAbout IU Cinema Creative Co
 llaborations Zoom Q&A + Prep Session\nRegistrants for this Q&A + prep sess
 ion will be able to speak with IU Cinema staff members regarding any quest
 ions related to the Creative Collaborations application process. \nCreativ
 e Collaborations enables groups at IU and in our community to highlight im
 portant topics and ideas through film screenings and film-related educatio
 nal programs with a mission of:\nFostering diverse programming partnership
 s that help bridge campus and community\nHighlighting critical issues and 
 themes through film-related and educational programs curated in collaborat
 ion with IU Cinema and subject-matter experts\nWelcoming new and returning
  audiences to IU Cinema\nCreative Collaborations is a competitive applicat
 ion process\, and any IU Bloomington unit\, student group\, Greater-Bloomi
 ngton community groups or non-profit organization is welcome to apply. Exp
 lore some of our previous Creative Collaborations programming to get an id
 ea of what past partners have presented.\nApplications for 2027–28 progr
 am proposals will be accepted from October 8–November 20\, 2026.\nFull p
 rogram guidelines are available at go.iu.edu/creativecollaborations. You c
 an register here for this Zoom Q&A and prep session!
