BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Breast Cancer Awaremess Walk
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261101T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261101T150000
UID:cf7f8d89d03f7bd5902a883a30b77e9e@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:Come out to Switchyard Park to support breast cancer awareness
  and support services for breast cancer patients and survivors. During the
  entire month of October\, we will Paint the Town Pink! Local businesses c
 an sign up to get their windows painted pink with ribbons and breast cance
 r awareness messages. Cancer Support Community is partnering with the City
  of Bloomington Parks and Recreation department\, IU Health\, and IU Schoo
 l of Medicine to provide resources and educational material to local busin
 esses. \n Awareness Saves Lives—Melody Martin started the Breast Cancer
  Awareness walk over 25 years ago\, because she believed had she gotten he
 r diagnosis sooner\, her outcome may have been different. We remember and 
 honor Melody's mission in life—to empower women to identify breast cance
 r sooner\, to have the best chance of survival. \n On November 1\, 2026 c
 ome to Switchyard Park from 1:00 - 3:00 pm for Paint the Town Pink celebra
 tion. The event will feature a Breast Cancer Survivor Ceremony\, followed 
 by a walk on Switchyard Park's half mile or one mile walking trail. Throug
 h the event educational materials and a resource fair will be available. F
 ood trucks will be onsite with some delicious local flavor. This event is 
 free and open to the public. Paint the Town Pink shirts are available thro
 ugh pre-registration. \n Donations to the walk support a local breast can
 cer support group\, SAVI bras for radiation patients\, and oncology massag
 es for breast cancer patients through Cancer Support Community. \n Surviv
 or Ceremony\nJoin us for one of the most meaningful moments of Paint the T
 own Pink—our Breast Cancer Survivor Ceremony\, beginning at 2:30 PM.\n D
 uring the ceremony\, each survivor will be invited to step onto the stage\
 , share their name and length of survivorship\, and be honored by the comm
 unity. As survivors exit the stage\, they will receive a small tribute gif
 t as a token of recognition and support.\n We ask all survivors to begin l
 ining up near the stage a few minutes before the ceremony begins so we can
  start on time.\n Last year\, we were honored to present embroidered Paint
  the Town Pink scarves to 34 survivors who joined us. This year\, we look 
 forward to celebrating even more stories of strength\, resilience\, and ho
 pe.
GEO:39.1496733;-86.5388079
LOCATION:Switchyard Park\, 1601 S. Rogers Street\, Bloomington\, IN 47403
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/breast-cancer-awaremess-walk/59
 890/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
