BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:We the People
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261101T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261101T180000
UID:9214203822cf0b27132fc81b626f3cbf@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:Join the Bloomington Symphony Orchestra as they perform a conc
 ert in recognition of our country’s 250th year. From the familiar square
  dance feel of Copland’s Hoedown\, to the soulful\, bluesy tonalities of
  Still’s Afro-American Symphony\, this concert explores what it means to
  be an American.\n4:15pm pre-concert talk\n5:00pm performance\nProgram:\nA
 aron Copland – “Hoe-Down” from Rodeo\nGary Powell Nash – “In Mem
 oriam Sojourner Truth”\nJennifer Higdon – All Things Majestic\nWilliam
  Grant Still – Symphony No. 1\, “Afro-American”\n“I travel the wor
 ld\, and I’m happy to say that America is still the great melting pot 
 – maybe a chunky stew rather than a melting pot at this point\, but you 
 know what I mean.” – Philip Glass\, 1999 NPR interview\nBSO Season Pas
 ses can be purchased until October 16th. Passes include discounted tickets
  to all 4 season concerts\, reserved seating\, and other benefits. To lear
 n more and purchase your Season Pass\, visit bloomingtonsymphony.com/seaso
 npass57
GEO:39.1662844;-86.5328085
LOCATION:Buskirk-Chumley Theater\, 114 E. Kirkwood Avenue\, Bloomington\, 
 IN 47408
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/we-the-people/59787/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
