BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Treasures of the Silk Road
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261116T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261116T180000
UID:c72720bca8d4911a3fe7352c961ceb00@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:The McCalla Center\, in collaboration with musician and schola
 r Shahyar Daneshgar\, celebrates the opening of its new exhibition Treasur
 es of the Silk Road on Friday\, September 25th\, 4:00 pm-6:00 pm EDT.\nThe
  exhibit features over 70 musical instruments from the Pastel-Daneshgar mu
 sical instrument collection\, with a focus on strings\, flutes\, and percu
 ssion from across Asia\, the Middle East\, and North Africa. Crafted from 
 wood\, snakeskin\, horsehair\, lambskin\, camel bone\, and other unique ma
 terials\, these instruments provide a compelling history of cultural and a
 rtistic exchanges that have led to the myriad musical sounds and styles th
 at permeate the world today. The opening event will feature remarks from t
 he collection owner\, Shahyar Daneshgar\, and will feature musical clips p
 rovided by the Lotus World Music & Arts Festival.\nShahyar Daneshgar is a 
 lifelong musician\, scholar\, and cultural ambassador whose passion for tr
 aditional music has shaped more than three decades of collecting\, teachin
 g\, and performing. Born into a large musical family\, he studied at the T
 ehran Conservatory of Music before pursuing academic work in Germany and l
 ater at Indiana University\, where he earned his Ph.D. in Central Eurasian
  Studies in 1995. He taught at Indiana University until his retirement in 
 2024. He is founder and director of the Bloomington Silk Road Ensemble.\nT
 he exhibition is free and runs from September 25\, 2026\, to September 202
 7.\nThe mission of the McCalla Center is to provide accessible exhibition 
 and educational experiences\, creating opportunities for students\, facult
 y\, and the community to engage with collections\, IU-generated creative a
 ctivity\, and community projects in meaningful and innovative ways.
GEO:39.1709246;-86.527549
LOCATION:McCalla Center\, McCalla Center\, 525 E. 9th Street\, Bloomington
 \, IN 47408
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/treasures-of-the-silk-road/5960
 4/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:2026 Monroe County Childhood Conditions Summit
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261116T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261116T163000
UID:98bf5476c989a9a201251bfd54c8fa43@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:YSB and BTCC are proud to host an 11th year of the Monroe Coun
 ty Childhood Conditions Summit exploring how we can shape what surrounds u
 s!\n Over the past decade\, the Summit has been guided by the concept that
  ‘ what surrounds us\, shapes us .’ Children and youth are shaped by t
 he relationships they are a part of\, the neighborhoods they live in\, the
  places they learn and play\, and the policies and practices developed by 
 the organizations and institutions with which their families interact.\n T
 he (CDC) developed a framework called  Essentials for Childhood  intende
 d for communities committed to the positive development of children and fa
 milies. When children have access to safe\, stable\, and nurturing relatio
 nships and environments (SSNREs) they are more likely to thrive - and thri
 ving children are more likely to grow into thriving adults. What we do as 
 a community and in the community affects those conditions.\n From safe and
  affordable housing\, to economic security\, to zoning\, to climate resili
 ence to healthcare access and beyond\, these social and structural determi
 nants impact the capacity of children and their caregivers alike\, to deve
 lop and thrive. When systems and the people within them are being stretche
 d\, what opportunities do we have to shape what surrounds us in a way that
  embeds safety\, stability and nurturance into our community?\n This year 
 at MC3 we are looking at opportunities to shape what surrounds us\, and we
  look forward to seeing you in November to build stronger relationships as
  individuals and organizations to and impact the conditions affecting kids
  and families in Monroe County and beyond!
GEO:39.1643817;-86.5355699
LOCATION:Bloomington Convention Center\, 302 S. College Avenue\, Bloomingt
 on\, IN 47403
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/2026-monroe-county-childhood-co
 nditions-summit/59889/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:KinderYoga - Baby & Mom Music & Movement
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261116T091500
